body:
![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

If `payload.reveal_gates.reveal_allowed_after` is present but is not an array (for example, an object like `{}`), `!Array.isArray(allowedAfter)` evaluates to `true` and pushes an error. However, the subsequent check calls `allowedAfter?.some(...)`. Since `{}` is not nullish, optional chaining evaluates `{}.some` to `undefined`, and attempting to call it as a function throws an unhandled `TypeError: allowedAfter?.some is not a function`.

To fail closed gracefully and prevent runtime exceptions, explicitly verify that `allowedAfter` is an array before calling `.some()`, or default it to an empty array.

```javascript
  let allowedAfter = payload.reveal_gates?.reveal_allowed_after;
  if (allowedAfter !== undefined && !Array.isArray(allowedAfter)) {
    pushError(errors, 'controlled_vocabulary_violation', 'reveal_gates.reveal_allowed_after', 'invalid reveal gate');
    allowedAfter = [];
  } else if (allowedAfter === undefined) {
    allowedAfter = [];
  } else if (allowedAfter.some((value) => !ENUMS.reveal_allowed_after.includes(value))) {
    pushError(errors, 'controlled_vocabulary_violation', 'reveal_gates.reveal_allowed_after', 'invalid reveal gate');
  }
  if (
    payload.ms_source_reveal?.manual_reveal_allowed === true &&
    !allowedAfter.some((value) => value === 'submitted_answer' || value === 'student_confirmed_attempt')
  ) {
    pushError(
      errors,
      'manual_reveal_without_attempt_confirmation',
      'reveal_gates.reveal_allowed_after',
      'manual reveal needs submitted answer or student confirmed attempt',
    );
  }
```

<details>
<summary>References</summary>

1. When adding robustness checks (such as optional chaining or Array.isArray) for potentially malformed or missing input data, include regression tests to verify that the system fails closed gracefully (e.g., returning a failure status) rather than throwing unhandled TypeErrors.
</details>

