If `exposed_neighbor_question_labels` is passed as a string (e.g., `"abc"`), it will have a `.length` property (e.g., `3`). If `exposed_neighbor_question_count` is also `3`, the count check will erroneously evaluate to `true` and bypass validation. 

To prevent silent mismatches and ensure robust validation, explicitly verify that `exposed_neighbor_question_labels` is an array using `Array.isArray` and default to an empty array if it is not.

```javascript
  const neighborLabels = Array.isArray(payload.page_exposure_risk?.exposed_neighbor_question_labels)
    ? payload.page_exposure_risk.exposed_neighbor_question_labels
    : [];
  if (payload.page_exposure_risk?.exposed_neighbor_question_labels !== undefined && !Array.isArray(payload.page_exposure_risk.exposed_neighbor_question_labels)) {
    pushError(errors, 'page_exposure_count_mismatch', 'page_exposure_risk.exposed_neighbor_question_labels', 'labels must be an array');
  }
  if (
    (payload.page_exposure_risk?.exposed_neighbor_question_count ?? 0) !==
    neighborLabels.length
  ) {
    pushError(errors, 'page_exposure_count_mismatch', 'page_exposure_risk.exposed_neighbor_question_count', 'count must match labels');
  }
```

